  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="b900-f71c-499c-e8d7" name="Cataphract (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>CATAPHRACT ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.26-27): Parthian, Palmyrene and Sassanid Persian armies, 50 BC - AD 600.
Characters: the army may have a General and an Army Standard Bearer. Cavalry at least a quarter of the points; Infantry up to half; Special Troops up to a quarter, with one artillery piece per 500 points and one elephant per 1,000 points.
Cataphracts: count their rank bonus up to a maximum of +3 and may not march.

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Cavalry: at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Special Troops: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
